Each line describes how one UTF-16 code unit is encoded in a text index
key: S (simple), I (international), U (unprintable), P (unprintable
modifier), Z (international with "crazy" flag), G (significant) or
X (ignored). Lines for U+0100 onwards skip the surrogate range.
